ZERO WEB0.15PREVIEW VERIFICATION
25 November2026

Implementation: original Zero only. No Chromium/V8/Python implementation was
copied or included. A cancelled experimental client-side Python worker was
removed after the user clarified server-side Python websites.

Original Zero automated checks
DOM170, CSS151, JavaScript320 and full document pipeline35:676checks per host.
Each suite passed native Linux x64 and as a Windows x64 binary under Wine.
The pipeline covers HTML/CSS/JS interaction, hidden subtrees, textContent,
background inheritance, inline backgrounds after script replacement, BR,
unsupported scripts, UTF-8 rejection, capacity, renderer guards and scrolling.
DOM/CSS/JS checks include deterministic malformed input and guard checks.
An independent DOM review exercised10000additional malformed inputs across
revisions; the final6000input run passed. These are testing samples, not proof
that every malformed page or every web standard is supported.

Independent integration review
67separate assertions passed:51CLI/format/layout cases,8composition cases and
8additional background/word-wrap/clipping cases. The review found and fixed
BR handling, inline backgrounds, the background after textContent replacement,
and missing-argument handling for single CLI options.
Own Zero renderer probes also passed deep200and maximal512nested nodes,
extreme CSS dimensions, memory guards and exact overlapping viewport pixels.

GUI
10interactive scenarios per platform passed on Linux/Xvfb and Windows/Wine.
The actual final browser's entire demonstration canvas matched its own
Zpix export pixel-for-pixel on both platforms. A40paragraph document scrolled
with PageDown and returned exactly with Home; Esc and native close exited.
Window-error/headless/renderer-error paths were checked. Native Windows hardware,
Wayland without Xwayland and physical devices are not verified by these tests.

Build and regression boundary
The standard original builder completed76stages and72artifacts. A build made
with the freshly built builder reproduced all72artifacts byte-for-byte.
The64previous0.14artifacts excluding the changed builder pair are byte-identical
to their prior baseline, including kernels, bootloaders, guest apps and ISO.
Boot code did not change; new BIOS/UEFI or VirtualBox runs are not claimed.
Private storage.zdrive and data.vdi hashes remain unchanged.

Scope
This is a tested local preview profile. It does not establish modern Internet
compatibility, complete HTML5/CSS/ECMAScript, TLS, process isolation or a full
Chromium rewrite. New guest integration and Internet fetching remain unfinished.
